\section{Source and formal scope}
The Pauli preliminaries state twisted commutation and Fourier cancellation for
an arbitrary prime field characteristic, using the additive character
$\omega^{\operatorname{tr}(\cdot)}$.  The landed QPBT operator definitions use
the binary character with phase $-1$, because the test fixes field sizes
$q=2^k$.  This unit therefore states the source-facing algebra with the
general character `ffChar` and keeps binary matrix corollaries under separate
names for downstream QPBT consumers.
